{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791051540,"nonce":"PIIicN5M6XuLrebhUubgKa/Qkoo=","title":"ZynML: host-class fields are accessor methods, not field syntax","message":"Host modules imported through TieredRuntime::add_host_modules expose a field x as c.x() / c.set_x(v) (static: C::x() / C::set_x(v)), because extern types have no field access in ZynML: process_extern_declarations_mut registers them with no fields, and field access on Type::Extern does not lower. Field syntax (c.x, c.x = v) needs field access on extern types routed to the type's accessor functions.","files":null}]}